  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Very warm start to the week, followed by mild conditions most of\n  the week. \n\n- Change to a cooler, moister pattern this weekend.\n\n- Snow potential coming late next weekend and early next week.\n\nThe weather will remain mild with temperatures about 15 degrees\nabove average through about Friday this week. Ensembles are\nshowing a trough move into the region this weekend and potentially\na back door cold front by Sunday. Confidence is very high for a\ncool down for this weekend. \n\nThe other impacts from this system are less confident. Ensembles\nare showing a very wide range of potential precipitation and snow\namounts for Saturday through Monday. Precipitation amounts vary\nfrom a few hundredths to inch across a wide swath of the forecast\narea. Most of those details depend on the track that the low\nultimately takes, which is highly uncertain at a 5-6 day lead\ntime. The areas most at risk of significant snow accumulations are\nalong the Continental Divide where the probability of 1 inch or\nmore of new snow is over 80 percent. The lower elevations of\nwestern Montana have chances ranging from 0-15 percent for 1 inch\nof snow, and the Clearwater and Nez Perce mountains in central\nIdaho range from 5-55 percent chance for an inch of snow by Monday\nmorning.",
